{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Journey Through Japan**\n\nLast spring, I embarked on a two-week adventure through Japan, a country where ancient traditions meet cutting-edge modernity. My journey began in Tokyo, where neon-lit streets and towering skyscrapers create a futuristic skyline. I explored Shibuya’s bustling crossing, visited the serene Meiji Shrine, and indulged in sushi at Tsukiji Outer Market.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the shinkansen (bullet train) to Kyoto, Japan’s cultural heart. There, I wandered through bamboo forests in Arashiyama, admired the golden Kinkaku-ji Temple, and participated in a traditional tea ceremony. The blend of history and tranquility was mesmerizing.\n\nNext, I ventured to Hiroshima, where I paid my respects at the Peace Memorial Park and Museum. The resilience of its people left a profound impact. A short ferry ride took me to Miyajima Island, home to the iconic floating torii gate of Itsukushima Shrine.\n\nMy final stop was Osaka, where I savored takoyaki and okonomiyaki in Dotonbori, a feast for the senses. The city’s vibrant nightlife and friendly locals made it a perfect send-off.\n\nJapan’s beauty lies in its contrasts—cherry blossoms against skyscrapers, quiet shrines amid neon chaos. Every moment was a discovery, and I left with memories to last a lifetime.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.10421782732009888}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.05028626695275307}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -1.7195216417312622}, {"token": " Through", "logprob": -0.20240268111228943}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.07294084876775742}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -3.010676145553589}, {"token": "Last", "logprob": -1.054956078529358}, {"token": " spring", "logprob": -1.729674220085144}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0001656871900195256}, {"token": " I", "logprob": -0.007762504741549492}, {"token": " embarked", "logprob": -0.4625747203